      altTranslation: "The servants who groan like a crow with a firebrand in its mouth —\nhaving seen the great-flower sacred feet of the one who rises from sleep:\nI shall praise the shining glory of the silver-white moon-faced one\nwho holds the hollow conch taken from the sea.",
      theme: "The Crow with Fire — devotees who have seen the Lord's waking feet groan like a crow with a burning brand in its mouth — joy and agony indistinguishable in the experience of grace.",
      note: "Koḷḷi vāyk kāgam — a crow with a burning coal/firebrand in its mouth — is an image of something simultaneously precious and unbearable. The devotee who has seen the Lord's feet is in this condition: the vision is too much, too hot, too bright, yet impossible to release. The burning coal of grace."
